From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:21:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mt6797-consys: start despite stale BTIF
 receive bytes

BTIF is outside CONN, so a CONN power-off leaves its FIFOs as they are. If
the firmware sent bytes nobody read, every later CONSYS start refuses with
-EBUSY before it sends anything, and only a reboot recovers. Station 30
reached this state after the GNSS link stopped with bytes pending.

Log those bytes, since they are the firmware's last words, and let the
existing clear remove them. A transmitter that is still busy stays a
refusal, now with a message. A start with an empty FIFO behaves as before.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt.h | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt.h b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt.h
index 8206b1506..07979eefe 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt.h
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt.h
@@ -839,6 +839,19 @@ static void mt6797_wmt_fifo_clear(void __iomem *base)
 	writel(readl(base + WMT_BTIF_IIR) & ~BIT(2), base + WMT_BTIF_IIR);
 }
 
+#define WMT_BTIF_STALE_MAX 64
+
+static void mt6797_wmt_stale_rx(void __iomem *base)
+{
+	unsigned char stale[WMT_BTIF_STALE_MAX];
+	unsigned int count = 0;
+
+	while (count < sizeof(stale) && (readl(base + WMT_BTIF_LSR) & 1))
+		stale[count++] = readb(base);
+	if (count)
+		pr_warn("mt6797-consys: %u stale BTIF bytes: %*ph\n", count, count, stale);
+}
+
 /*
  * Caller holds the shared CONSYS lock, after fresh power/reset release and
  * before HIF or a sleep command. No transport retry or shutdown is attempted.
@@ -873,10 +886,17 @@ static int mt6797_wmt_query_setup(struct mt6797_wmt_query *query)
 	if (query->deadline_supplied && time_after_eq(jiffies, query->deadline))
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 
-	/* Normal bank first; reject nonempty FIFOs before any clear. */
+	/* Normal bank first. BTIF outlives a CONN power-off, and with it whatever
+	 * the firmware sent last: keep those bytes in the log, then clear them.
+	 * A transmitter still busy is refused.
+	 */
 	writel(0, query->btif + WMT_BTIF_FAKELCR);
-	if ((readl(query->btif + WMT_BTIF_LSR) & 0x41) != 0x40)
+	mt6797_wmt_stale_rx(query->btif);
+	if (!(readl(query->btif + WMT_BTIF_LSR) & 0x40)) {
+		pr_err("mt6797-consys: BTIF transmitter busy: LSR=0x%02x\n",
+		       readl(query->btif + WMT_BTIF_LSR));
 		return -EBUSY;
+	}
 	/* One admitted timeout acknowledgment if auto-reset was off. */
 	dma = readl(query->btif + WMT_BTIF_DMA_EN);
 	if (dma & (BIT(0) | BIT(1)))
